bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_tuple_pattern_bare_fieldless_variant_binds_hir_types_equal_true_2026-11-12, 0, "2026-11-12 OPEN. Rust seed native codegen treats a BARE fieldless enum variant inside a tuple pattern (case (Str, Str), case (Red, Red)) as a catch-all binding; qualified (Kind.Str, Kind.Str) and payload variants work. Pure-Simple compiled code is correct. Impact: every Stage 2 binary is seed-compiled, so hir_types_equal (src/compiler/20.hir/hir_lowering/type_equality.spl:74, case (Bool, Bool): true is the first bare fieldless arm) returns true for any pair not caught by the Int/Float arms - measured arr_str/sl_str/bool_str/u8_str all true on seed vs false on pure-Simple. Every hir_types_equal caller on the Stage 2 lane (merge joins, payload agreement) is silently lax. Evidence: doc/08_tracking/bug/seed_tuple_pattern_bare_fieldless_variant_binds_hir_types_equal_true_2026-11-12.md."

